/*
  AIoT SMART LAUNCH RISK ASSESSMENT
  ESP32-WROOM-32D

  Hardware:
    - 2 x HX711 + 1 kg load cell (left and right)
    - MPU6050 (I2C)
    - Analog resistive water-level sensor (inside model)
    - u-blox NEO-6M GPS (UART2)
    - 2-pin active buzzer driven by NPN transistor
    - 2 x HC-SR04 (one entry gate, one exit gate)

  Required Arduino libraries:
    - HX711 by Bogdan Necula (or compatible bogde HX711 library)
    - TinyGPSPlus by Mikal Hart

  Notes:
    - HC-SR04 ECHO pins MUST use 5V-to-3.3V voltage dividers.
    - Buzzer is driven through an NPN transistor, not directly by GPIO.
    - Water percentage is a relative sensor-coverage estimate, not litres.
    - One HC-SR04 per gate detects an approach event; it cannot reliably
      determine direction or guarantee a person fully crossed the gate.
    - This is a model/prototype monitor, not a certified launch safety system.
*/

